<title>USA: Times.</title>
<headline>Times.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange censured and fined brokerage D.H. Blair $250,000 for not supervising brokers whose forceful sales techniques generated customer complaints, the New York Times said Thursday.</p>
<p>Blair consented without admitting or denying guilt to findings of sales-practice misconduct, the paper said.</p>
